    "created_at": "2026-09-13T10:23:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-13T10:23:18Z",
    "body": "It looks like the empty line after the empty-but-tagged value is getting parsed as a line before the empty value. Here's a minimal example; the custom-ness of the tag is irrelevant here:\n\n```js\nconst src = '- x: !!null\\n\\n- y'\nparseDocument(src).toString()\n```\n\n```yaml\n- x:\n\n    !!null\n- y\n```\n\nThis also happens with anchors:\n\n```js\nconst src = '- x: &a\\n\\n- y'\nparseDocument(src).toString()\n```\n\n```yaml\n- x:\n\n    &a\n- y\n```\n\nAnd it seems specific to the last key-value pair of a mapping inside a sequence, as this is correct:\n```js\nconst src = '- x: !!null\\n\\n  y'\nparseDocument(src).toString()\n```\n\n```yaml\n- x: !!null\n\n  y:\n```\n\nCalling the resulting YAML \"bogus\" is a bit miseleading, though, as it's still valid.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
